xmss — provenance note
======================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling
`bip340`/`slhdsa`/`falcon` modules — self-contained crypto modules not
folded into the root NOTICE).

Provenance
----------

xmss — clean-room implementation from RFC 8391 ("XMSS: eXtended Merkle
Signature Scheme", IRTF, May 2018), covering: the hash-address scheme
(Section 2.5), base_w (Section 2.6), WOTS+ (Section 3.1), the XMSS
single-tree scheme (Section 4.1: RAND_HASH, L-trees, treeHash, keygen,
sign, verify), the SHA-256 function instantiations (Section 5.1) and the
XDR wire formats (Appendix B). RFC 8391 is a public specification; the
algorithms were implemented from the RFC text.

Test-vector oracle: the official XMSS reference implementation,
https://github.com/XMSS/xmss-reference (the code referenced by RFC 8391
Section 7; CC0/public-domain per its LICENSE). It was used as a
BLACK-BOX oracle only — built unmodified and driven by a small local
generator with fixed deterministic inputs to produce the byte-exact
known-answer vectors embedded in src/kat_vectors.zig (primitive outputs,
WOTS+ keys/signatures, XMSS public keys and signatures at h = 2, h = 4 and
h = 10 — h = 2 added to byte-anchor a full sequential stateful-index walk
of all-but-the-last one-time key, see kat_vectors.zig for why the tree's
final leaf is excluded). No source code from xmss-reference was ported into the module;
two implementation-defined conventions were intentionally matched for
interoperability and are documented in SPEC.md: (a) the NIST SP 800-208
PRF_keygen WOTS+ secret-key derivation (toByte(4, 32) domain prefix),
and (b) the keypair seed layout sk_seed || sk_prf || pub_seed used by
the KAT generator.

No other third-party source was ported or consulted. Uses only the Zig
standard library (std.crypto.hash.sha2.Sha256).

Intended first consumer: SCADA firmware signing (IEC 62443-style
code-signing chains standardized around NIST SP 800-208 stateful
hash-based signatures).
